WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.968
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.590
NARRATOR: Invented in
the early 19th century

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.020
by a Scottish scientist
studying light,

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.910
the kaleidoscope
can still compete

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.300
when it comes to producing
stunning visual effects.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.530
Peer inside and witness dazzling
geometric images produced

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.150
as mirrors multiply objects.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.220
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.890
The images are
spectacular and fleeting,

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.724
each one lasting just seconds
before the next appears.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.880
Many years after its
invention, the kaleidoscope

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.420
is still worth looking into.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.290
To make a kaleidoscope,
this craftsman

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.790
starts with the mirror sheet
that has adhesive backing.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.120
He scores it to create
long and narrow rectangles

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.360
and gently breaks it
along the scored lines.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.670
The mirror's reflective
coating is on the front

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.650
instead of the underside.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.320
A mirror like this produces
sharper reflections

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.840
than a regular household mirror.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.810
He slices the adhesive
backing to separate

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.100
the mirrored rectangles.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.670
He snaps off the
scored ends, creating

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.935
perfectly linear edges.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.810
Next, he peels backing
from a strip of blackout

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.770
felt paper and wraps it
around a glass rectangle.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:23.410
This felt wrapped glass
will be the third wall

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.500
of the two mirror system,
one with a triangular

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.340
configuration.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.080
He removes the adhesive
film from the mirrors,

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.120
then builds the triangles
with the mirror's

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.340
reflective surfaces
facing inward

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.200
towards the
felt-wrapped rectangle.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.500
This arrangement
will reflect objects

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.360
to create a circular
image known as a mandala.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.300
He aims the mirrors
system at a light box

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.250
with a two line drawing in it.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.710
One line is curved and
the other is straight.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:59.080
Peering into it, he adjust
the alignment of the mirrors

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.750
until the lines morph
into a five point star.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.530
This means the corners
of the mirror triangle

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:08.650
are precisely 36
degrees and it is

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.479
multiplying images correctly.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.590
He hot glues the mirrors
to the opaque part

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.480
and applies metal
tape to the top

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.210
seem to complete the
kaleidoscope mirror system.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.410
Over in the art
department, the artist

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.380
assembles decorative objects
against a black background

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.385
and an acrylic cell.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.240
With every placement, she
checks the effect through

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.545
the triangular mirror system.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.470
She glues dichroic
glass onto the backdrop.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:40.900
It's a kind of glass that's
been treated with metal oxides

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.655
and it appears to
have different hues.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.440
Other objects include
jewelry parts, colored wire,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.360
buttons, and even paper clips.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.610
She follows no specific
design but works free style.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.500
While she glues some
down, she leaves others

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.985
loose to simply tumble around.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.730
A sprinkle of tiny beads
completes the grouping.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.250
As the mirror system
multiplies these objects,

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.540
they will create the mandalas.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.670
These are photographs
of actual mandalas,

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.860
and they'll be used to
decorate the outside

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.870
of the kaleidoscope.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.910
The other member of
the team now applies

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.640
an acrylic adhesive
to the rim of the cell

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.460
and presses a clear lid onto it.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:32.650
The lid fuses to the
cell body, but it's

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.690
not yet completely sealed.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.150
There's a tiny hole in
the side of the cell

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.360
through which he now
dispenses heavy mineral oil.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.820
Submerged in mineral
oil, the objects

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.310
will float and move through
the cell for greater effect.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.480
He plugs the hole with an
acrylic adhesive and screw.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.200
He is now ready to assemble all
the parts of the kaleidoscope.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.180
He slides the mirror system
into a heavy cardboard

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.510
tube decorated by
the mandala photos.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.790
He cushions the mirror
system with foam,

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.190
and this stabilizes it.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.269
He installs a metal eyepiece
and glass lands on one

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:19.829
end of the kaleidoscope too.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.720
He slides the object cell
into a protective metal

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.650
cage that rotates.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:32.130
He places a transparent
glass disk over the cell.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.430
He applies adhesive to
the cage and inserts

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:39.370
the assembly into the other
end of the kaleidoscope tube.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.480
This kaleidoscope is
now ready for a viewing.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.260
Light passes through
the object cell,

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.120
illuminating the trinkets.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.920
Reflections bounce
off the mirrors

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.040
to create one spectacular
illusion after another.

00:04:55.525 --> 00:04:58.240
Two centuries after
its invention,

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.700
the view through the
kaleidoscope still fascinates.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.050
[MUSIC PLAYING]

